# The committed client build is an artefact, not source. Git normalises line
# endings in anything it thinks is text, which would rewrite the bundle on
# every checkout - different bytes on Windows and Linux for the same commit,
# and a served file that is not the one that was built. Nothing here is edited
# by hand, so nothing here should be touched.
/client/dist/** -text -diff

# Source art is binary and large. Marking it stops git trying to diff a 2048px
# PNG and stops any chance of a checkout mangling one.
/art/** -text -diff
*.png binary
